---
import ArticleLayout from "../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import MatchCard from "../../../src/components/React/MatchCard";
import "../../styles/global.css";

// Logos
import WorldCupLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/World-Cup.svg";

import MexicoLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/Mexico.svg";
import SouthAfricaLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/south-africa.svg";

import BrazilLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/Brazil.svg";
import MoroccoLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/Morocco.svg";

import NetherlandsLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/Netherlands.svg";
import JapanLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/Japan.svg";

import FranceLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/France.svg";
import SenegalLogo from "../../../public/World-Cup/Senegal.svg";
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="World Cup Preview MD1 & My Predictions - 5/6/2026"
  date="June 5, 2026"
  author="Konstantinos Chaldoupis"
  tags={["WorldCup", "Predictions"]}
>
  <p>
    The 2026 World Cup is just around the corner, and the excitement is
    palpable! With 48 teams set to compete across North America, this tournament
    promises to be one of the most thrilling in history. As we gear up for the
    kickoff, let's take a look at some of the key matchups and my predictions
    for how things will unfold.
  </p>

  <h2>Key Matchups to Watch in Matchday 1</h2>
  <p>
    A rematch of the 2010 opening match happens again as Mexico faces South
    Africa this time around in Mexico City Stadium hoping to get the full 3
    points this time.
  </p>

  <MatchCard
    client:load
    homeTeam="Mexico"
    awayTeam="South Africa"
    homeScore={0}
    awayScore={0}
    competition="Group Stage - Group A"
    competitionLogo={WorldCupLogo.src}
    status="UPCOMING"
    homeLogo={MexicoLogo.src}
    awayLogo={SouthAfricaLogo.src}
    kickoffTime="2026-06-11T22:00:00+03:00"
  />

  <hr />
  <br />

  <p>
    One more exciting matchup to look forward to is the clash between Brazil and
    Morocco in Group C as two of the best teams in each confederation play each
    other that might decide first place and runner up of this group.
  </p>

  <MatchCard
    client:load
    homeTeam="Brazil"
    awayTeam="Morocco"
    homeScore={0}
    awayScore={0}
    competition="Group Stage - Group C"
    competitionLogo={WorldCupLogo.src}
    status="UPCOMING"
    homeLogo={BrazilLogo.src}
    awayLogo={MoroccoLogo.src}
    kickoffTime="2026-06-14T01:00:00+03:00"
  />

  <hr />
  <br />

  <p>
    Another exciting matchup is the clash between the Netherlands and Japan in
    Group F with both teams having met once before in the 2010 World Cup where
    Netherlands clinched on the 3 points thanks to a goal from Wesley Sneijder
    and an assist from Robin van Persie.
  </p>

  <MatchCard
    client:load
    homeTeam="Netherlands"
    awayTeam="Japan"
    homeScore={0}
    awayScore={0}
    competition="Group Stage - Group F"
    competitionLogo={WorldCupLogo.src}
    status="UPCOMING"
    homeLogo={NetherlandsLogo.src}
    awayLogo={JapanLogo.src}
    kickoffTime="2026-06-14T23:00:00+03:00"
  />

  <hr />
  <br />

  <p>
    A battle of former colonies is on as France takes on Senegal. The meeting
    carries deep historical weight, with many of France's own players having
    family ties to Senegal. On the pitch, it's a clash of generations — European
    efficiency versus African flair — both fighting for pride and progression.
  </p>
  <MatchCard
    client:load
    homeTeam="France"
    awayTeam="Senegal"
    homeScore={0}
    awayScore={0}
    competition="Group Stage - Group I"
    competitionLogo={WorldCupLogo.src}
    status="UPCOMING"
    homeLogo={FranceLogo.src}
    awayLogo={SenegalLogo.src}
    kickoffTime="2026-06-16T22:00:00+03:00"
  />

  <hr />
  <br />

  <p>
    These are just a few of the many exciting matchups to look forward to in the
    2026 World Cup. With so much talent on display and the stakes higher than
    ever, it's anyone's guess who will come out on top. I can't wait to see how
    it all unfolds!
  </p>

  <h2>My Predictions</h2>

  <MatchCard
    client:load
    homeTeam="Mexico"
    awayTeam="South Africa"
    homeScore={2}
    awayScore={0}
    competition="Group Stage - Group A"
    competitionLogo={WorldCupLogo.src}
    status="PREDICTION"
    homeLogo={MexicoLogo.src}
    awayLogo={SouthAfricaLogo.src}
  />

  <MatchCard
    client:load
    homeTeam="Brazil"
    awayTeam="Morocco"
    homeScore={1}
    awayScore={1}
    competition="Group Stage - Group C"
    competitionLogo={WorldCupLogo.src}
    status="PREDICTION"
    homeLogo={BrazilLogo.src}
    awayLogo={MoroccoLogo.src}
  />

  <MatchCard
    client:load
    homeTeam="Netherlands"
    awayTeam="Japan"
    homeScore={0}
    awayScore={0}
    competition="Group Stage - Group F"
    competitionLogo={WorldCupLogo.src}
    status="PREDICTION"
    homeLogo={NetherlandsLogo.src}
    awayLogo={JapanLogo.src}
  />

  <MatchCard
    client:load
    homeTeam="France"
    awayTeam="Senegal"
    homeScore={2}
    awayScore={0}
    competition="Group Stage - Group I"
    competitionLogo={WorldCupLogo.src}
    status="PREDICTION"
    homeLogo={FranceLogo.src}
    awayLogo={SenegalLogo.src}
  />
</ArticleLayout>
